{
  "storyId": "B-914f",
  "name": "routine-validate-fresh-pass-reuse",
  "title": "Reuse fresh routine validation PASS evidence on unchanged material",
  "description": "Prevent ordinary lattice validate and REVIEW-to-TEST validation from re-executing an unchanged validation plan when a trustworthy PASS already exists. B-c163 evidence showed 5 redundant successful re-runs on identical materialHash+storyFilesHash costing 1,926,151ms (32.10 minutes); B-19ca reproduced the control-flow gap when 45/45 commands passed but stale verification coverage forced a second identical 370-second execution after evidence refresh. Implement a fail-closed reuse decision using shared trusted metadata lineage plus a routine validation identity that binds command specs, entrypoint digests, focus/full/profile, and verification-policy inputs. Legacy/malformed/mismatched evidence must execute; reuse must occur inside the validation lock with HEAD recheck and must not rewrite evidence or create metadata commits.",
  "type": "feature",
  "phase": "REVIEW",
  "priority": "high",
  "riskSignals": [
    {
      "category": "Validation Framework",
      "matched": "lattice validate"
    }
  ],
